{"files":[{"content":"#include \"knn.h\"\n\ntypedef struct {\n    float distance;\n    char label;\n    size_t ordinal;\n} Neighbor;\n\nstatic int neighbor_is_worse(const Neighbor *a, const Neighbor *b) {\n    if (a->distance > b->distance) return 1;\n    if (a->distance < b->distance) return 0;\n    return a->ordinal > b->ordinal;\n}\n\nstatic void heap_sift_up(Neighbor *heap, size_t index) {\n    Neighbor value = heap[index];\n\n    while (index != 0) {\n        size_t parent = (index - 1) / 2;\n        if (!neighbor_is_worse(&value, &heap[parent])) break;\n        heap[index] = heap[parent];\n        index = parent;\n    }\n\n    heap[index] = value;\n}\n\nstatic void heap_sift_down(Neighbor *heap, size_t heap_size, size_t index) {\n    Neighbor value = heap[index];\n\n    while (index < heap_size / 2) {\n        size_t child = 2 * index + 1;\n        if (child + 1 < heap_size &&\n            neighbor_is_worse(&heap[child + 1], &heap[child])) {\n            child++;\n        }\n        if (!neighbor_is_worse(&heap[child], &value)) break;\n        heap[index] = heap[child];\n        index = child;\n    }\n\n    heap[index] = value;\n}\n\nstatic char vote_labels(char *labels, int k) {\n    qsort(labels, k, sizeof(char), compare_for_sort);\n\n    char most_frequent = labels[0];\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\n    int current_frequency = 1;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i < k; i++) {\n        if (labels[i] != labels[i - 1]) {\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n                most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n            }\n\n            current_frequency = 1;\n        } else {\n            current_frequency++;\n        }\n\n        if (i == k - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n            most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n        }\n    }\n\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n\nstatic char knn_linear(int n_groups, Group *groups, int k,\n                       Point to_evaluate, char *labels) {\n    float *distances = (float *)malloc(sizeof(float) * (size_t)k);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        labels[i] = -1;\n        distances[i] = -1;\n    }\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        Group g = groups[i];\n\n        for (int j = 0; j < g.length; j++) {\n            float d = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, g.points[j]);\n\n            for (int x = 0; x < k; x++) {\n                if (d < distances[x] || distances[x] == -1) {\n                    for (int y = k - 1; y > x; y--) {\n                        distances[y] = distances[y - 1];\n                        labels[y] = labels[y - 1];\n                    }\n\n                    distances[x] = d;\n                    labels[x] = g.label;\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    char result = vote_labels(labels, k);\n    free(distances);\n    return result;\n}\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group *groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    char *labels = (char *)malloc(sizeof(char) * (size_t)k);\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        labels[i] = -1;\n    }\n\n    size_t heap_capacity = (size_t)k;\n    size_t point_count_capped = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups && point_count_capped < heap_capacity; i++) {\n        if (groups[i].length > 0) {\n            size_t group_length = (size_t)groups[i].length;\n            size_t remaining = heap_capacity - point_count_capped;\n            if (group_length >= remaining) {\n                point_count_capped = heap_capacity;\n            } else {\n                point_count_capped += group_length;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    heap_capacity = point_count_capped;\n\n    Neighbor *heap = NULL;\n    if (heap_capacity != 0) {\n        heap = (Neighbor *)malloc(sizeof(Neighbor) * heap_capacity);\n    }\n\n    size_t heap_size = 0;\n    size_t ordinal = 0;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        const Group *g = &groups[i];\n\n        for (int j = 0; j < g->length; j++) {\n            Neighbor candidate;\n            candidate.distance = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, g->points[j]);\n            candidate.label = g->label;\n            candidate.ordinal = ordinal;\n\n            if (candidate.distance != candidate.distance) {\n                free(heap);\n                char result = knn_linear(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate, labels);\n                free(labels);\n                return result;\n            }\n\n            if (heap_size < heap_capacity) {\n                heap[heap_size] = candidate;\n                heap_sift_up(heap, heap_size);\n                heap_size++;\n            } else if (heap_capacity != 0 &&\n                       neighbor_is_worse(&heap[0], &candidate)) {\n                heap[0] = candidate;\n                heap_sift_down(heap, heap_size, 0);\n            }\n\n            ordinal++;\n        }\n    }\n\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < heap_size; i++) {\n        labels[i] = heap[i].label;\n    }\n\n    free(heap);\n    char result = vote_labels(labels, k);\n    free(labels);\n    return result;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n    Group *groups = (Group *)malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n}","path":"src/knn.c"}],"hypothesis":"A bounded max-heap reduces top-k maintenance work while traversal ordinals preserve earlier-point precedence for equal distances. Capping heap storage at the point count avoids excess heap allocation; rerunning the original scan on a NaN distance preserves its ordering behavior. The controller should evaluate the integrated program's correctness and speed.","notes":"Only src/knn.c is changed. The original label sort and plurality vote are retained; no parallel path is added.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":["b671e999abac4de6","e499a157e6f74ad7"],"transformations":["Replace per-point top-k scans and shifts with a contiguous max-heap, storing traversal ordinals to preserve earlier-point precedence on equal distances; cap heap capacity at min(k, total point count).","If a computed distance is NaN, rerun the original ordered scan. Preserve the existing label sort and plurality vote."]}